# ==============================================================================
# Mosquitto ACL File — Example
# ==============================================================================
# Topic access per device login. Copy to 'acl' (no .example extension, kept out
# of git) and restart the broker: docker compose restart mqtt
#
# It applies to the device listeners (MQTT_PORT, MQTT_WS_PORT, MQTT_TLS_PORT)
# once MQTT_USER and MQTT_PASSWORD are set in .env. The stack's own services
# (Node-RED, Telegraf, the ai stack) use the internal listener on p4n4-net and
# aren't affected, and the MQTT_USER account always has access to every topic.
# An account with no matching line here can't publish or subscribe at all.
#
# Topics (README: MQTT Topic Convention):
#   sensors/<device-id>/<measurement>      readings
#   inference/<device-id>/result           edge inference results
#   sandbox/...                            the same, written to the sandbox bucket
#   commands/<device-id>/...               commands to a device (by convention)
#
# Permission levels: read (subscribe), write (publish), readwrite (both).
# In "pattern" lines, %u is the login's username and %c its client ID.
# With MQTT_READONLY_USER configured, global write patterns are refused:
# they would also grant that account permission to publish.
# ==============================================================================

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Example device: repeat this user block for each device's login and ID.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
user sensor-001
topic write sensors/sensor-001/#
topic write inference/sensor-001/result
topic write sandbox/sensors/sensor-001/#
topic read commands/sensor-001/#

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Read-only monitoring account (e.g. dashboards, MQTT Web UI for operators)
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
user monitor
topic read sensors/#
topic read inference/#
topic read system1/#
topic read $SYS/#

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Operator account that sends commands to devices
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
user operator
topic read #
topic write commands/#
